Transport leg also requires transport_leg_available (initially true). After assembly, transport_leg_available becomes false.

After assembly, we need to authorize transport leg loading: authorize_transport_leg_loading requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we need origin_availability linked to a task profile. We have origin_availability_alpha with task profile linked (we attached earlier). Good.

Thus after assembling leg, we can authorize loading.

Now we need to load container beta onto leg: load_container_onto_leg requires candidate_prepared ?candidate (beta), candidate_transport_leg_linked ?candidate ?transport_leg, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_available ?loading_container, transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg, not loading_container_loaded ?loading_container.

We have candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha (init). candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta (init). loading_container_beta available initially. So after leg assembled and loading authorized, we can load container.

After loading, we get loading_container_loaded true, loading_container_leg_linked true, loading_container_available false.

Now we need candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta: we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal (since destination leg not loaded). Precondition: candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, loading_container_leg_linked? Actually includes loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, (not destination_leg_loaded ?transport_leg), not candidate_loading_verified. So we need candidate_staged_for_loading first.

Candidate_staged_for_loading precondition: candidate_prepared ?candidate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_loaded ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate.

Thus we need loading_container_loaded and leg linked (we will have after load), task profile linked to beta, operator linked, skill certificate linked, and not origin_leg_loaded (we haven't loaded origin leg). So after loading container onto leg, we can stage.

Thus steps for beta after leg assembled and loading authorized:

